1. raise "msg" makes a RuntimeError
   RuntimeError: "just a message"
2. raise Klass makes an instance whose message is the class name
   ArgumentError: "ArgumentError"
3. raise Klass, "msg"
   ArgumentError: "with a message"
4. raise Klass.new("msg"); and raise obj, "msg" replaces the message
   ArgumentError: "an instance"
   ArgumentError: "replaced"
5. a bare raise inside rescue re-raises the same object
   outer got IOError: "inner"; same object: true
6. a bare raise outside any rescue: a RuntimeError with an empty message
   RuntimeError: ""
7. a third argument sets the backtrace
   e.backtrace ["frame_a", "frame_b"]
   with caller: the first entry is in "Object#validate", not in check
8. fail is an alias of raise
   RuntimeError: "fail is raise"
9. raising something that is not an exception
   TypeError: "exception class/object expected"
   TypeError: "exception class/object expected"
   TypeError: "exception class/object expected"
10. $! and $@ inside rescue, and after it
   $!.equal?(e)            true
   $@.equal?(e.backtrace)  true
   $! after the rescue     nil
11. raise Klass, args calls Klass.exception(*args)
   Custom.exception called with []
   Custom: "Custom"
   Custom.exception called with ["msg"]
   Custom: "msg"
